   We assume one site measures without a boundary $e^{-φ(x)}dx/Z$ that satisfy a log-Sobolev inequality. We prove that if these measures are perturbed with quadratic interactions, then the associated infinite dimensional Gibbs measure on the lattice always satisfies a log-Sobolev inequality. Furthermore, we present examples of measures that satisfy the inequality with a phase that goes beyond convexity at infinity.

